    "result_text": "There's only one test class (plus `AcceptanceBase` and likely a config helper). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `capacityWarning` flag on owner responses.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only boolean `capacityWarning` to the `OwnerDto` schema (mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`). Since DTOs are generated from this spec, this produces the `setCapacityWarning`/`getCapacityWarning` accessors.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40`.\n   - Added `isCapacityWarningActive(String city)`, which counts owners in the city (using the same normalized, case-/whitespace-insensitive grouping as the existing `rejectCityAtCapacity`) and returns `true` when the count is in `[40, 50)` \u2014 i.e. 40\u201349 owners.\n   - Set `capacityWarning` at all three response sites that already set `bulkSignupWarning`: `getOwner`, the idempotent-replay create path, and the create path.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`rejectCityAtCapacity` \u2192 HTTP 409) is untouched; the warning window is strictly below it.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass (including the new `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` acceptance test, which fills a city to 40 and asserts the 41st owner reports `capacityWarning: true`).",
